{"object_id":"org.acb290b0843b31ec","object_type":"network","slug":"blue-network","title":"Blue Network","paragraphs":["The Blue Network began as NBC's second national service. After it was separated from NBC in the 1940s, it became the foundation of what soon became ABC.","In Golden Radio Hour, [[org|org.acb290b0843b31ec|Blue Network]] is tied to 12 programs. The surviving network-linked recordings here run from 1935 to 1945.","Programs with a particularly strong presence here include [[show|lum-and-abner|Lum and Abner]], [[show|the-green-hornet|The Green Hornet]], [[show|duffys-tavern|Duffy's Tavern]], [[show|old-gold-comedy-theater|Old Gold Comedy Theater]], [[show|inner-sanctum-mysteries|Inner Sanctum Mysteries]], [[show|fibber-mcgee-and-molly|Fibber McGee and Molly]], [[show|gang-busters|Gang Busters]], [[show|i-love-a-mystery|I Love a Mystery]], [[show|counterspy|Counterspy]], and [[show|the-lone-ranger|The Lone Ranger]].","People who recur often in those network-linked recordings include [[person|chester-lauck|Chester Lauck]], [[person|norris-goff|Norris Goff]], Lou Crosby, George W. Trendle, Lee Allman, Gilbert Shea, Rollon Parker, Charles D. Livingstone, Bob Hite, and Al Hodge. These are archive connections, not a claim that everyone on the list was employed directly by the network."],"plain_text":"The Blue Network began as NBC's second national service. After it was separated from NBC in the 1940s, it became the foundation of what soon became ABC.\n\nIn Golden Radio Hour, Blue Network is tied to 12 programs. The surviving network-linked recordings here run from 1935 to 1945.\n\nPrograms with a particularly strong presence here include Lum and Abner, The Green Hornet, Duffy's Tavern, Old Gold Comedy Theater, Inner Sanctum Mysteries, Fibber McGee and Molly, Gang Busters, I Love a Mystery, Counterspy, and The Lone Ranger.\n\nPeople who recur often in those network-linked recordings include Chester Lauck, Norris Goff, Lou Crosby, George W. Trendle, Lee Allman, Gilbert Shea, Rollon Parker, Charles D. Livingstone, Bob Hite, and Al Hodge. These are archive connections, not a claim that everyone on the list was employed directly by the network.","word_count":136,"quality_tier":"rich","evidence_features":["network_history","network_program_links","shows","people"],"show_count":12,"linked_episode_count":610,"person_count":12,"shows":[{"series_id":"series.lum_and_abner_384e6538","title":"Lum and Abner","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":408,"first_date":"1935-09-17","last_date":"1945-06-14","slug":"lum-and-abner"},{"series_id":"series.the_green_hornet_049a79ad","title":"The Green Hornet","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":89,"first_date":"1939-11-25","last_date":"1945-05-31","slug":"the-green-hornet"},{"series_id":"series.duffy_s_tavern_f4a5c000","title":"Duffy's Tavern","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":39,"first_date":"1943-01-05","last_date":"1945-11-30","slug":"duffys-tavern"},{"series_id":"series.old_gold_comedy_theater_0ddb600b","title":"Old Gold Comedy Theater","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":30,"first_date":"1944-10-29","last_date":"1945-06-10","slug":"old-gold-comedy-theater"},{"series_id":"series.inner_sanctum","title":"Inner Sanctum Mysteries","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":10,"first_date":"1941-01-07","last_date":"1943-03-07","slug":"inner-sanctum-mysteries"},{"series_id":"series.fibber_mcgee_and_molly_31d3e470","title":"Fibber McGee and Molly","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":7,"first_date":"1935-12-09","last_date":"1936-05-18","slug":"fibber-mcgee-and-molly"},{"series_id":"series.gang_busters_8fa8f770","title":"Gang Busters","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":7,"first_date":"1940-11-01","last_date":"1944-06-09","slug":"gang-busters"},{"series_id":"series.i_love_a_mystery_aace0e3b","title":"I Love a Mystery","relation_type":"broadcast_on_network","episode_count":7,"fi